      "math_academy_id": "q-225004",
      "sequence_position": 10,
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(10)$ given below, compute $P(X=7).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0103\\,$ | $\\,0.0293\\,$ | $\\,0.0671\\,$ | $\\,0.1301\\,$ | $\\,0.2202\\,$ | $\\,0.3328\\,$ | $\\,0.4579\\,$ |\n\n$P(X=7)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(7) & =P(X\\le 7) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,7\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,6\\})+P(X=7) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 6)+P(X=7) \\\\  & =F(6)+P(X=7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=7) & =F(7)-F(6) \\\\  & =0.2202-0.1301 \\\\  & =0.0901.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
